NAME
       dd - copy blocks between files and devices

SYNOPSIS
       dd [if=FILE] [of=FILE] [bs=N] [count=N] [skip=N] [seek=N]
          [status=none]

DESCRIPTION
       Copies data block by block, which makes it the tool for reading
       and writing raw devices.

OPERANDS
       if=F      read from F (default standard input)
       of=F      write to F (default standard output)
       bs=N      block size in bytes (default 512; K, M, G suffixes)
       count=N   copy only N blocks
       skip=N    skip N blocks of input first
       seek=N    skip N blocks of output first
       status=none  do not print the transfer summary

EXAMPLES
       dd if=/dev/sda of=/mnt/mbr.bin bs=512 count=1
       dd if=/dev/zero of=disk.img bs=1M count=64

SEE ALSO
       hexdump(1), mkfs(1)
